{
  "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
  "title": "Offline simulation v1: signals, sequences, and Boolean triggers",
  "description": "Version 1 offline model. Constants retain their original semantics. Ramps use finite binary64 arithmetic at sample timestamps. Runtime checks exact tag/type matching, bounds, generator coverage, and strict integer tokens; dry-run separately applies point/byte limits and checks generated arithmetic. Staircases use positive whole-millisecond durations and explicit holdLast behavior; runtime also checks cumulative duration overflow. Random duration ranges require an explicit uint32 seed; optional maxTotalDurationMs reserves remaining minima. Runtime checks ordered ranges and budget feasibility. Random integer holds fill durationMs exactly; runtime validates schedule feasibility, value ranges, and hold allocation limits. Sequences compose finite staircase and random-integer schedules on local clocks. Runtime checks cumulative duration overflow and shared allocation limits. Boolean switches require a declared local Boolean constant or timeline; runtime binds dependencies and prevents unsupported input types. Boolean gates omit closed slots; pause or continue after first true. Runtime validates source binding; preview pointCount counts emitted points while its limit applies to candidate slots. String timelines hold exact string values; SKU routes compare them case-sensitively and require readiness. Runtime validates direct source types and rejects duplicate route claims for the same sources and SKU.",
